WEBVTT

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.700
What the hell is this?

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.180
And you call yourself a professional?

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:20.950
Some dreamy-eyed young apprentice would be more useful than an unmotivated bum like you.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.350
What is it that you want to do?

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.220
Didn't you ever have a dream?

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.380
You're quitting?

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.960
That's why you were calling chefs from other restaurants.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.760
I certainly can't count on you to do that.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.310
Don't ever set foot in there again.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:52.820
Are you still going to have a job here the next time I drop by?

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.620
<i>Some stay and some go.</i>

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.190
<i>The restaurant holds people's histories within them.</i>

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.470
<i>Various personalities have mixed...</i>

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.780
<i>in this restaurant that sits on a corner of Rome.</i>

00:02:56.710 --> 00:03:01.180
Day Off from the Ristorante

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:01.100
So it's really broken?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.470
I thought it felt a little cold in here.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.620
When will it be fixed?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.970
Tomorrow, at the earliest.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.000
It could be until the following day.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.730
If it's just one day, I think it'll be fine.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:19.320
It's been pretty warm lately.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.490
No, to be safe, we should close for the day.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:27.340
I'll explain it to the customers who made reservations.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.720
We can't have anyone catching a cold now.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.070
Hey there.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.790
Buon giorno.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.990
Have you put some thought into the new menu?

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.490
You bet I did!

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.670
It looks like the market beat us to spring.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.860
I'm delighted to be thinking up the new menu.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:08.940
Say, I thought up a dish. If it's really good...

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.880
You want to see if it'll end up on the menu?

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.820
I remember.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.180
But, I don't think that's gonna happen.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.770
Oh, come on! We won't know until I try!

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:19.780
I know, I know.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:33.730
<i>I've got to start with the very basics.</i>

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.970
Grilled scampi.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.560
Veal sirloin.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.340
Frittatas.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.210
Buon appetito.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:16.560
You know, if you kick the flavoring up a notch, I think it'll work.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.870
I agree 100%.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:21.450
If you marinated the meat a bit longer, and lightened up the sauce just a bit...

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.950
Guys, taste mine too!

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.290
With no further ado.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.610
The presentation is nice...

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.110
...but it tastes like crap.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.240
M-M-Maybe I overcooked the eggs...

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.600
You lack fundamentals.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:53.630
Th-That's because you won't teach them to me!

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:56.130
Didn't you graduate culinary school?

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.620
Learn them on the job, by yourself.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:04.120
Now, guys... There's no need to overcomplicate matters.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.510
Well, you need to work on your plating!

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.020
Gigi plated it.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.350
<i>Wh-When did he...</i>

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.520
Gigi, is the technician still going to be a while?

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:21.890
G-Gigi, you prefer more attractive plating, don't you?

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:23.790
All that matters is the taste.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.330
Something smells delectable.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:31.680
Claudio! Did you come to support me?

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:34.320
I wanted to see how the repairs are coming.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.630
I'm glad we closed for the day.

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:38.250
It's freezing today.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.980
Are you sure you didn't close because you can't stand a little cold?

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:44.420
A lady gets cold easily!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.510
Claudio is just considerate of that.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.260
Oh, right! Claudio!

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.050
Yes?

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.370
Come here!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.600
Taste this.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.140
Sure.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:01.800
Well?

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.640
Well, it looks really nice.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.760
Looks nice, huh?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.670
Yes, but it looks really nice.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:12.850
Looks nice...

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:21.190
<i>This is delicious!</i>

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.690
<i>I'll get 'em this time!</i>

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:33.740
<i>I've been observing their techniques closely!</i>

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:44.600
Pollo alla Diavola.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:48.090
Artichoke in cream sauce.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.370
Roasted lamb served with crispy potatoes.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:54.240
Buon appetito.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:04.130
Teo, you should use a little more salt.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.910
Maybe it'll go better with porcini mushrooms.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:10.140
<i>Oh my... This is delicious!</i>

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.540
<i>How come they can make such delicious food?</i>

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.840
<i>They must have some secret in their arms!</i>

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.180
It's not just their arms.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.770
They both started to eat your dish, Nicoletta.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:24.650
What?!

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.150
It's not <i>bad</i>...

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.030
It just defies sense.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:40.660
S-Sure, maybe we can't serve it to the customers,

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.780
but maybe the staff could eat it, no?

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.850
Sure, but...

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:47.060
This is a ristorante!

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.430
This belongs in a mess hall!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.090
It's too salty.

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:09.600
Sure it's just not to your tastes?

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:12.350
You aren't considering the customers at all.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.620
I don't know what mess hall you trained in,

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.420
but this is a ristorante.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.530
You need to relearn everything.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.410
You can go straight to hell!

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.000
What's so bad about this dish?

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.600
The owner said it's good.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.000
It's identical to the specialty at a restaurant I went to recently.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.510
You're imagining things.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:35.900
Quit making excuses and think up a new dish.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:41.570
Screw her!

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:16.030
That is a letdown.

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:18.940
I wouldn't worry about it too much.

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:21.090
Teo just has a foul mouth.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:25.540
We used to really worry about Teo too, back in the day.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:26.080
Huh?

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:30.020
He was uninspired and always fighting with the head chef.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.350
Teo?

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.000
Yeah.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.690
He caused all sorts of headaches for us.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.380
Why the culinary world?

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:06.010
I lived with my grandparents when I was a child.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:09.980
I absolutely loved my grandmother's cooking.

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.700
How about you, Teo?

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:16.240
My father was a chef before he passed away.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.850
What? In a ristorante?!

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.420
It was just a tiny osteria.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.250
Did you ever cook for him?

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.300
Yes.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.620
I bet he was thrilled at how delicious it was!

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.410
Sure, I guess.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.310
Huh?

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:35.420
He wasn't a straight-shooter either.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.170
In a ristorante back home...

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.000
In a two-star restaurant in Rome...

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:45.980
He trained for years and never improved.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.410
He had the makings of a good chef, though.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.600
I wanted to help him out somehow.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:54.720
That's why I asked him to work in dell'orso.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:56.420
I remember it well.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.890
I bluntly told him that at least his dolces were good.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:07.530
Teo used to want to show his father that he could make it.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:13.420
But, he lost sight of his goals along with the passing of his father.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:19.000
They say the master will appear when the pupil is ready, but...

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:22.680
I guess meeting lots of people is a great thing in itself.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:24.380
Definitely.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:27.550
Back when Teo and Vanna were going at it,

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:30.720
he was like a rebellious child!

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:38.270
<i>Everyone starts off as an amateur.</i>

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.230
<i>I'll make them say it's delicious!</i>

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.470
Make food that you like yourself.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:45.650
Huh?

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:48.040
<i>Is he talking to me?</i>

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:56.220
<i>Maybe I'll try some potatoes with cheese.</i>

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.030
You're using bottarga!

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:07.160
What kind of fish?

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.190
Mullet.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.560
It's because he grew up in Sardinia.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.800
Oh, that's a nice area!

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:17.170
Bottarga, aragosta, Pecorino cheese...

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:21.520
Teo was brought up on rich ingredients from the mountains and the sea.

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:23.450
It was just a town out in the country.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:29.460
The basis of a man's culinary tastes come from the type of food culture they were brought up in.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.690
The wife and I talk about this all time.

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:36.440
One of these days, we want to have our own food tour of Italy.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:38.800
That sounds like so much fun!

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.210
There's probably all sorts of good food in Italy.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:46.150
There are ingredients we've never even heard of in different parts of the country.

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.110
I wouldn't mind traveling around on my motorcycle.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:53.350
Of course, nothing tops Sardinia.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.160
<i>He hasn't really talked about it,</i>

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.530
<i>but I wonder if Teo has a special someone in his life.</i>

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.280
<i>He uses ingredients from back home...</i>

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:14.430
<i>I bet they make him think about his late father, too.</i>

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.700
Make food that you like yourself.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.820
<i>I wonder how many years it's been since I made this.</i>

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:31.370
Grandma!

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:38.010
This is incredible.

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:39.950
It's delicious!

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:43.410
Wrapping it in a pie crust... Furio never ceases to amaze.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:46.490
Well then, next is Teo's dish.

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:57.710
How is it?

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.160
Delicious!

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:00.830
Absolutely delicious!

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:05.420
Nicoletta, you've said every plate is delicious so far.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:10.710
I'd like a more delicate and rich response from a woman chef.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:16.310
But, Nicoletta's facial expressions are more delicate and rich than words can convey.

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:22.090
I'd love you to try and top the old woman chef.

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:25.420
Woman chef? There used to be one here?

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.680
What?! I thought that was a man!

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.410
That's Vanna.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:36.110
Teo and her were always going at it.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.660
It was downright frightening.

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:41.520
So...

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:45.040
She ended up quitting because of him?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.620
No, it was because of her family.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.540
They moved to America.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:52.490
She's a top-rate chef.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.530
Up next is Nicoletta's dish.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:05.390
<i>I think this is the best I've made so far,</i>

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:06.530
<i>but...</i>

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:10.180
Buon giorno!

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.440
I heard you're thinking up the spring menu?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.700
It looks fabulous!

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.760
Buon appetito!

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.380
Delicious!

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:23.230
I can't get enough of that crispy pie crust!

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.530
This is lovely too.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:31.020
Huh?

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:35.720
This tastes oddly... familiar...

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.650
Nicoletta.

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:44.970
This would be considered very good,
had it been made by a layperson.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:46.120
However...

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.990
A pro can do better.

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:56.380
You're right.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:58.540
Home cooking is good,

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:00.850
but it doesn't fly in a restaurant.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.460
Thank you for being so honest with me.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:04.250
Huh?

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.840
I learned an awful lot today!

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:09.380
Skills are important,

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:13.550
but I think it's also important to think about the people eating your dishes.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.220
I think the next dish I make will be even more delicious!

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.160
I'll... go clean up.

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:34.080
She got a little full of herself.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:44.940
Thank you.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:53.560
There's a saying that us cameriere believe in.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.350
Hmm?

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:57.840
A restaurant that serves good food to the staff is a good restaurant.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:05.550
You even got Teo to honestly admit it was good.

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:10.100
I'm so glad!

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:27.400
Is it really OK for us to go home while the boiler is still being worked on?

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:29.990
We'll let Gigi worry about it, so it's fine.

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:32.630
It'll get even colder once night falls.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.680
Indeed.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:50.050
<i>Huh? Isn't that Teo's motorcycle?</i>

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.150
Did you figure out the menu?

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.310
Sure did.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.000
Huh?

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:55.780
Long time no see.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:59.060
It's been some time.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:00.040
It sure has.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.280
This is Vanna.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:04.820
What?!

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:08.180
Ahh!

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:10.950
What's this all about?

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.220
You must be Nicoletta.

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:15.580
Piacere.

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:18.300
They told me you were in America.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.620
I'm going back next week.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:22.560
It's a shame you can't stay longer.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:25.380
I'll come by to try out the new menu.

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:26.590
Please do!

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:28.640
I heard that you're a top-rate chef!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.670
Who on earth said such a silly thing?

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.040
See you tomorrow.

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:39.080
Ciao.

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:46.890
<i>Could those two be...</i>

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.420
My wife's waiting at the enoteca.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.290
Care to join us?

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.730
I have to go home and practice!

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:57.760
I had a tough time today.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:02.510
You want to be acknowledged as being a good professional chef, don't you?

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:03.920
You called it!

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:04.980
Ciao!

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:21.030
You know, I'll think I'll take you up on that drink!

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.220
There's no reason for me to rush.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.010
Right?

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:26.750
We'd love for you to join us.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:21:15.980
Secret Love

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:59.350
Looks like I am without a rival.

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:07.250
Or am I mistaken?

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:57.980
You want to watch again next time... Or am I mistaken?
